{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/49577-cheiron-logo","id":49577,"title":"Cheiron Logo","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-14T22:59:05-08:00","id":49577,"title":"Cheiron Logo","content":"So the art in the books have never actually showed the Cheiron group logo that is alleged to be &quot;satanic&quot;. It's described as a bearded, horned man with a laurel wreath over a caducas. I had an idea, drawing on the old Proctor &amp; Gamble logo (the inspiration source for Cheiron's logo issues) and the idea that the &quot;new&quot; logo (the minimalist bow and arrow show in the book) is a simplification of their official one. Here's a crude draft.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://pic100.picturetrail.com/VOL769/2851441/23895100/408560073.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> My idea is that they had some deniability on the &quot;horns&quot; because the face formed a crescent moon (or bow) ala the old Proctor and Gamble logo. The caduceus is the arrow &amp; drawn bow string. I went with one snake for Aesclepius rather than Hermes, but left the wings because it does technically say caduceus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T02:16:09-08:00","id":49637,"title":"","content":"I want to say the stylized bow and arrow are for just the bag-and-tag division; page 136 for the core says their manual has the bow and arrow symbol, but no corporate logo. If the bow and arrow were riffing off the corporate logo, it will kill the ability to deny it easily. I always assumed the logo was a Green Man-esque face, full-on, with the snake-staff behind it. Mainly because it is described as being on ancient artifacts, and the Greeks went for full-face grotesqueries, while profile distortions tends to be something you see in Victorian and art nouveau style illustrations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T11:22:04-08:00","id":49935,"title":"","content":"I like the way phalamir is thinking here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatcher